the  origin of the idea was just how do you  make the luxury bridal experience  accessible  to the 99 i'm molly king i'm the founder  and ceo of floravera and i graduated  from the gsb class of 2015.  so florivera were on a mission to really  revolutionize the entire bridal industry  by offering  luxury bridal gowns and a truly luxury  intimate private experience for shopping  for your gown with  radical price points that have never  existed before  so it's been a while since i've seen  that video  yeah it's kind of blowing my mind the  difference  how i don't even know however many  months since we did this can make  how drastically what your life looks  like can change is  is kind of sad and probably going to  make me emotional  you know you have all these big dreams  and plans  and we had so many things planned for  2020 you know we were operating for four  years but really two years in earnest  and we had  opened 13 showrooms in 13 different  cities across the u.s  and then in march 2020  kovit happened and  practically overnight we closed all of  our showrooms  and the state of weddings in general in  the u.s  was suddenly in limbo you know it's it's  ironic to look back in my early pitches  to investors i always said the beauty of  this business is that it's  recession-proof because people will  always be getting married  but it was not pandemic proof my  professor one of my professors from the  gsb  he was sort of the one that mentored me  through my second year and really  convinced me to launch this business  he said to me you know molly in in life  and career  success is often just timing and luck  and so you were at the wrong place at  the wrong time but he said mark my words  six years from now seven years from now  there will be an incredibly successful  business that looks just like yours  the part about it that surprised me  through this time was  how supportive my investors were through  that time  and then they then turned around and  said what do y